# CR 707.10: a copy of a spell copies the additional costs paid for it. Bot1 casts Requiting Hex with blight at Bot2's Llanowar Elves
# (the counter on Bot1's Ornithopter), then flashes in Lutri, the Spellchaser, whose enters trigger copies the Hex, aimed at the same
# Elves. The copy resolves first and destroys it, gaining 2 life because its additional cost was paid; the original's target is gone,
# so it does nothing (CR 608.2b). Bot1 ends at 22: a copy that had not paid the cost would have gained nothing (and the original, which
# has, never resolves).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Black Lotus
Ornithopter
Requiting Hex
Lutri, the Spellchaser
Island x3
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Llanowar Elves
Island x5
Island x13

[Actions]
